= Homeostasis — Simple =

'''Homeostasis''' means keeping important conditions inside a living body or cell within workable ranges while the world around it changes.

For example, when you get hot, sweating can help cool you down. Cells also need ways to control the salts and other substances inside them.

Many of these controls use [[Feedback|feedback]]: the body notices a change and acts to reduce it. The body is not frozen in place; its cells continually use energy and exchange materials.

